  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Boeing obligated $5.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Boeing received 473 awards so far, with an average award size of $12.4M, and obligations were up 34.4% year over year. Boeing’s fiscal-year obligations show variation: FY21 $7.3B, FY22 $3.9B, FY23 $3.3B, FY24 $5B, FY25 $4.4B, and FY26 $5.9B. The Department of Defense is the primary buyer, obligating $5.9B to Boeing in FY2026 to date. Boeing’s work is concentrated in Aircraft Manufacturing, which accounted for $5.8B of obligations in FY2026 to date. Other measurable markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing $63.5M, Engineering Services $6.4M, Computer Systems Design Services $3.3M, Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing $506K, Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals $173K, and Hardware Manufacturing $7.9K. The current-year totals are fiscal year to date, so the FY2026 numbers are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Boeing’s FY2026 federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $5.9B to Boeing in FY2026 to date. Aircraft Manufacturing accounted for $5.8B of Boeing’s FY2026 to-date obligations. Other NAICS markets for Boeing are much smaller, with the next largest being Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing $63.5M and Engineering Services $6.4M. Computer Systems Design Services, Search and Detection systems, and precision instrument manufacturing together amount to modest obligations listed on the page."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have Boeing’s federal obligations trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Boeing’s obligations ranged from FY21 $7.3B down to FY23 $3.3B, then rose to FY24 $5B and FY25 $4.4B, and reached $5.9B in FY26 to date. Boeing’s FY2026 to-date obligations are up 34.4% year over year. Boeing received 473 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $12.4M. The series shows variability across the listed fiscal years."
      }
    ]
  },
